Getsome wrote:
> I'm having a hard time figuring out the weapon charts
> http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/weap-341.html
> It would seem that only a Quarterstaff & a Dagger are good weapons for a 
> Wizard?
> What weapon should I be looking for? 

	Magicbane. You're guaranteed it as your first sacrifice-gift,
and it'll be better than anything else you're likely to get your hands
on until mid-game or so.

	Failing that, a stack of daggers for throwing. (Really, you want
those anyway.) I usually wield the starting quarterstaff until I get
Magicbane, but don't bother advancing the quarterstaff skill... the
skill points are more useful later for spell skills, and I won't use a
quarterstaff again after I've gotten Magicbane. I *do* train up dagger
as quickly as possible... wizards can get Expert in daggers, which makes
them a machine gun of death, and they become my primary offense until I
get the Eye and can rely on my spells.

